# Worktrees
.worktrees/

# Generated data (do not commit raw or projection parquet)
# `data/raw/*`, not `data/raw/`: git cannot re-include a file whose parent DIRECTORY is
# excluded, so a trailing-slash pattern would make the negation below silently do nothing.
data/raw/*
# The id map is the exception: 125K of reference data (gsis_id <-> name/position/team) that
# both live boards require to start. Without it a fresh clone cannot run them at all, which
# is the one thing a non-technical user cannot debug.
!data/raw/id_map.parquet
data/features/
data/projections/
data/backtest/
data/backtests/
data/diagnostics/
data/manifests/
data/sanity_checks/
data/external_projections/
data/draft_sessions/
data/auction_sessions/
data/dfs_universe_*.parquet
*.duckdb

# Trained model artifacts (joblib pickles; reproducible from source + data)
models/artifacts/
*.joblib

# Optuna study databases — artifact-of-search; tuned JSON is the artifact-of-decision
data/tuned_params/optuna_studies.db
data/tuned_params/optuna_studies.db-journal

# One-off probe-validation artifacts (uncommitted)
scripts/_one_off_*.py
data/features_probe/

# Probe / adoption-gate stderr capture (LightGBM warnings etc; transient)
reports/*.stderr

# hero-vs-bots eval (resumable per-cell checkpoints + derived results)
_hero_*/
data/backtest/hero_eval/

# --- Local scratch and regenerable artifacts -------------------------------
# Research checkpoints, sweep outputs and generated preset tables. All are
# reproducible from scripts; none belong in history. Patterns are deliberately
# narrow so they do not shadow the tracked inputs that live alongside them --
# data/vorp_2026/will_half12.parquet and data/processed/consensus_projections/.
.superpowers/
_crashdump/
_h2h_ckpt_*/
data/_vorp_*.parquet
data/consensus_vorp_*.parquet
data/processed/espn_weekly_projections/
data/vorp_*/*team.parquet
data/vorp_*/*team.league.json
reports/_*/
reports/*.png

# ESPN private-league cookies — never commit
configs/espn_credentials.json

# League pulls. This repo is public and these carry real people's names, ESPN display
# handles and (in espn_raw.json) their SWID account ids. Kept local by decision
# (user, 2026-08-24). Regenerate with `python -m projections.ingest.espn_league`.
# ...except the two files the live draft board needs to configure itself, which carry only
# league RULES and file paths -- no member names, no ids, no cookies. Without them a second
# machine silently falls back to a generic preset (3 WR / 13 rounds / slot 1 / now_or_never),
# which is every default the profile exists to correct. Verified clean before un-ignoring;
# re-check by hand before adding any further file from this directory.
#
# Ignoring `data/leagues/` outright would make those exceptions dead letters -- git does not
# descend into an excluded DIRECTORY, so a `!` rule under one can never match. The contents
# are excluded instead, with the directories themselves left traversable.
data/leagues/*
!data/leagues/*/
data/leagues/*/*
!data/leagues/*/league_config.json
!data/leagues/*/board_profile.json
# Encrypted league docs (scripts/league_doc_cipher.py). Only ciphertext -- the matching
# plaintext keeps its own name and stays ignored by the rule above. Encrypt-then-MAC under a
# passphrase that is not in this repo. Still: nothing goes in here that would be a problem
# published, because the phrase is the only thing standing between it and the world.
!data/leagues/*/*.enc
